|WKO=====================================================================
|YKOCyberware is machinery grafted into your own body. An installed
implant grants its bonuses - stats, resistances, or chance-based "proc"
effects - for as long as it stays inside you.

Every implant occupies one or more body locations: eyes, ears, brain,
skull, jaw, throat, neck, spine, heart, lungs, torso, skin, shoulders,
arms, hands, legs, and feet. Only one implant may occupy a location.

Implants also strain the body. No implant can cost more than 10 strain, and
the 24 cyberware locations create an absolute capacity of 240. Your natural
limit starts at 6 and grows with your level: +1 per 10 levels, plus larger
bonuses at levels 50, 100, 150, 200, and 250. Cyber-touched origins grant
+2 strain each, to a maximum of +10. Each remort closes part of the distance
between your natural limit and 240, reaching full capacity at remort 50.
You cannot install an implant that would push your total strain past your
limit, and an implant may demand a minimum level or stranger things before
your body accepts it.

World cyberware is built in four broad qualities. Standard chrome offers
dependable basic benefits; refined chrome is more efficient or specialized;
military chrome carries stronger combat systems; and artifact chrome can
transform a build at the maximum strain cost or several body locations.
Quality does not replace item level: hardware recovered deeper into Tekal is
generally stronger even when it shares a grade with earlier equipment.

|WKBCommands:|YKO
  |YKBcyberware            |YKOShow installed technological implants, occupied
                       body locations, and cybernetic strain.
  |YKBcyberware <player>   |YKOWizards may inspect a currently connected
                       player's installed cyberware and strain.
  |YKBimplants             |YKOShow every object-backed implant by family,
                       including cyberware and bound relics.
  |YKBcyberscan <implant>  |YKOInspect an implant's type, grade, locations,
                       strain, visibility, and procs before installing.
                       Street Samurai receive additional contract details for
                       signature hardware. Their own installed implants also
                       show integrity, fragmentation, firmware effectiveness,
                       software issues, and recommended maintenance actions.
  |YKBinstall <implant>    |YKOInstall an implant you are carrying.
  |YKBextract <implant or location>  |YKORemove an installed implant,
                       returning it to your inventory. Alias: |YKBuninstall|YKO.

Installation and extraction require a staffed ripperdoc clinic, and the
ripperdoc will not operate while you are fighting. The Forbidden Replacement
Table in Nethrys Undercity's Ripperdoc Quarter is a formal clinic. You may use
|YKBengage ripperdoc|YKO there to review carried or installed hardware, see
the exact service fee, and confirm a procedure. You may use |YKBcyberware|YKO
and |YKBcyberscan|YKO anywhere.

Street Samurai diagnostics are private. A carried signature implant shows its
contract requirements and hardware profile, but current maintenance state
appears only when that exact implant is installed in the scanning Street Samurai.
Ordinary implants and scans by other players retain the standard report.

Installation costs 10,000 coins per point of implant strain, with a 10,000
coin minimum. Extraction costs 5,000 coins per strain, with a 5,000 coin
minimum.

Installed implants cannot be dropped and stay with you across sessions. They
are hidden from normal inventory while installed, but remain visible through
|YKBcyberware|YKO or |YKBimplants|YKO. Implant grade does not change this:
standard, refined, military, and artifact chrome all persist normally.

Only an implant explicitly created as temporary or nonpersistent is excluded,
and normal clinic installation rejects hardware that cannot be preserved. A
saved implant may also be temporarily unavailable if its blueprint cannot load
or a one-of-a-kind implant is already active elsewhere; its installation record
is retained for a later retry. Only active restored implants consume strain, so
missing or inactive hardware releases its strain automatically.

Relics and other non-technological implants can occupy the same anatomical
slots, but do not consume strain unless their own rules say otherwise.
Some implants are outwardly visible - anyone who looks at you will see
them - while hidden ones stay your secret. Procs trigger on their own
in combat: on your hits, when you take damage, when you are badly hurt,
or when you make a kill, each with its own chance and cooldown.

General Tekal forbids cybernetics, so recoverable implants are uncommon and
normally expose an illicit source: contraband wetware dealers and surgeons,
augmented criminals, Green Door and Reca operatives, forbidden experiments,
or repurposed machinery. Rarer grades are normally found on specialists,
elites, or named threats. Shimmerdeep's Miura do not implant themselves;
cyberware recovered there comes only from corrupted external machinery and
mechaplants.

